cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Team MEEMAR's submission to the FPL'26 FPGA Design Optimization
  Contest: a cost-aware post-placement FPGA timing optimizer
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kamoliddin
    family-names: Fatkhiddinov
    email: misteruzbekguy@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/randomuzbek/meemar-fpl26-optimizer'
abstract: >-
  A post-placement FPGA timing optimizer built for the FPL'26 FPGA Design
  Optimization Contest. The contest scores max(0, alpha - 0.1*alpha*(beta +
  gamma)), where alpha is the f_max improvement in MHz, beta is LLM spend in US
  dollars and gamma is wall-clock hours, so compute is charged at a rate
  proportional to the gain it is chasing. The optimizer makes that trade
  explicit at runtime: a deterministic prepass ladder does most of the work and
  banks every proven improvement to disk, a legality and rollback layer makes an
  illegal or regressed output structurally impossible, and a language-model
  stage runs only when a break-even calculation says the remaining seconds will
  pay for themselves. The submission scored 318.254 across seven benchmarks with
  zero disqualifications and 7/7 clean legality, placing in the top five, with a
  total LLM spend of 0.35 US dollars.
keywords:
  - FPGA
  - physical design
  - timing optimization
  - placement
  - Vivado
  - RapidWright
  - design space exploration
  - LLM agents
  - cost-aware search
license: Apache-2.0
